diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ffc07e0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Chat Bots
+
+Bots are chat members that post messages via an HTTP API. They are implemented
+as STI subclasses of `User` (`Bot < User`), so they reuse memberships, messages,
+avatars, broadcasts, and push notifications exactly as humans do.
+
+## Model
+
+- `Bot < User` with `type = "Bot"`, `bot_code` (secure token, unique), and
+  `creator_id` (the human who created the bot).
+- `User.humans` (`type IS NULL`) vs `User.bots` / `Bot` scopes. Account lists,
+  sessions, transfers, and bans are scoped to humans; room membership UIs
+  include bots so they can be added like people.
+- `has_secure_token :bot_code` generates a URL-safe credential. Filtered from
+  logs via `filter_parameters`.
+- Bots get a random password on creation (email stays `nil`, so they cannot
+  sign in) and auto-join open rooms via `User#grant_membership_to_open_rooms`.
+- `User#can_administer?(bot)` is true for admins or the bot's creator, matching
+  rooms/messages authorization.
+
+## UI
+
+- Account settings (`/account/edit`) links to `/bots` via the bot icon
+  ("Set up chat bots", both nav icon with `aria-label` and a visible button).
+- `BotsController` (`/bots`, `/bots/new`, `/bots/:id/edit`):
+  - `index` lists `Bot.active.ordered` (all for admins, own for members) on one
+    page without pagination. Each `<li>` shows the name, a read-only
+    "Bot code" field, and an "Edit <name>" link.
+  - `new`/`edit` share `_form` with avatar (optional file) and "Name the bot"
+    (required label + placeholder + aria) plus "Save changes" submit.
+  - `edit` also has "Delete this chat bot" (`button_to … data-turbo-confirm`,
+    i.e. native `confirm()`). Destroy deactivates the bot user (preserves
+    messages, removes memberships), so the code becomes `401`.
+
+## API
+
+`POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_code/messages` (`Bots::MessagesController`):
+
+- Skips session auth (`allow_unauthenticated_access`) and CSRF
+  (`skip_forgery_protection`) for shell/CI use.
+- Raw request body (any `Content-Type`) becomes the message body after
+  UTF-8 forcing/scrubbing. No JSON envelope.
+- `401` if `Bot.active.find_by(bot_code:)` misses (checked first).
+- `404` if room missing or bot not a member (hides private rooms).
+- `422` if body blank (no attachment path for bots).
+- `201` with `Location: /messages/:id` (top-level `message_path`) on success.
+- Creates `room.messages.create!(body:, creator: bot)` then
+  `broadcast_create`; `after_create_commit → room.receive` handles unread +
+  `PushMessageJob`, identical to human messages. Author display uses
+  `message.creator` (the bot).
